--- !u!114 &1832169213
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1832169209}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 673caeaf093b68d4aa06d0eab062bd3c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuestGiver
  _prompt: Talk
  _speakerName: Marcus
  _defaultPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 430454738e079154685c22d8735cb403, type: 3}
  _idleLines:
  - I don't have anything for you right now.
  _stages:
  - label: JustExtract
    quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 781c8b233bb36c246a945363c3b57953, type: 2}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 0}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems:
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: de20da7781018d249be47a49efe908b9, type: 2}
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8a627e3eae018c14a8f5213081b99024, type: 2}
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - '*He looks up from his papers as you get close.*'
    - You make the face of a person who has no other choice.
    - Then sign this. It says you work until the job is done, not until it gets uncomfortable.
      Until it's done. Ya hear?
    - Down those stairs is what the city registered as a maintenance sewer. I need
      to know what's actually in there. I'm not sending you in armed, I'm not sending
      you in prepared - I just need eyes. Go in, take a look around, and come back
      out. That's it.
    - The sewers are that way. Come find me when you're back.
    inProgressLines:
    - Just take a look will ya?
    doneLines:
    - So tell me, what did you find?
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: FindMeScrap
    quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 428cee19d47ac5d489777ff84ed629a3, type: 2}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 781c8b233bb36c246a945363c3b57953, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems: []
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - '*He leans forward slightly*'
    - ...No light at all? Not emergency strips, not maintenance lamps, nothing?
    - He sits back. Quiet for a moment.
    - "That's not a maintenance sewer. Maintenance sewers have lighting \u2014 it's
      code. Someone stripped it out. Someone didn't want people to see what's down
      there."
    - He opens a case under the table and sets a flashlight and a small battery on
      the surface
    - "Take these. The flashlight runs on batteries \u2014 standard ones like this
      are single-use. Once they're dead, they're dead. You buy more from Kedr.\"
      He nods at the trader. \"Cheap, but you'll burn through them fast if you're
      not careful."
    - "There are rechargeable batteries too. Kedr carries them sometimes. They're
      expensive \u2014 rare, because whatever's down there drains them faster than
      it should. Normal batteries too, actually, which is why the single-use ones
      die so quick. Rechargeables at least you can top up at the station over there."
    - He points to the recharge station near the wall.
    - "Manage that battery. If it dies in there, you won't see a thing \u2014 and
      trust me, you do not want to be blind down there.\""
    - "Now. I want to know what else is in there. Go back in, pick up anything that
      looks sellable \u2014 garbage, scrap, whatever you find \u2014 bring me three
      things. Let's see what this place is actually hiding."
    inProgressLines:
    - go, go, just stay safe.
    doneLines:
    - Okay nicely done.
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: Savemoney
    quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bc6d614716a9b0a4582dba1e9e488021, type: 2}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 428cee19d47ac5d489777ff84ed629a3, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems: []
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - Not bad. Scrap, but it's sellable. Take it to Kedr, he'll pay you for it. Dont
      forget to buy some ammo and a mag
    - "From here on, you fund yourself. Batteries, supplies \u2014 that comes out
      of your earnings. I'm not your accountant."
    - "*A pause. His tone shifts slightly \u2014 not softer, but more serious.*"
    - There's something else I need to tell you. There are creatures down there.
      I don't know what they are yet. But they're there.
    - "People who took work like this before you \u2014 some of them didn't come
      back. I'm telling you that not to scare you, but because I need you alive.
      You're no use to me dead."
    - "So I want you armed. Kedr sells a Makarov \u2014 it's cheap, it's reliable,
      and it'll do the job. Save up a 150 credits and buy it."
    - "And until you have it \u2014 if you see anything moving down there that isn't
      your own shadow, you turn around and walk back to the exit. Don't run, don't
      engage. Just leave and try again."
    - The sewers aren't going anywhere. Come back when you have the money.
    inProgressLines:
    - dont spend your saved up money yet.
    doneLines:
    - "You have the money. Go buy the Makarov from Kedr \u2014 you're going to need
      it."
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: Survive5min
    quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2fcee74aaa6dd604397845f1dfbb968a, type: 2}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bc6d614716a9b0a4582dba1e9e488021, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems: []
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - Once you have it, I need you to start going deeper. But before that I want
      to know you can actually last down there. Not a quick look and out. Real time,
      real pressure.
    - "You've been running on one battery at a time. That won't cut it. Stock up
      from Kedr \u2014 enough to last five minutes without sweating every shadow.
      Then get down there and stay down there. Five full minutes before you extract"
    - Think of it as getting comfortable with the dark.
    inProgressLines:
    - nope that does not cut it. i need 5 minutes.
    doneLines:
    - Still alive. Good.
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: KillAnyQuest
    quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8b1ef5b631ffbeb4a838facc350e2886, type: 2}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bc6d614716a9b0a4582dba1e9e488021, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems: []
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - "You've seen enough of the outer section. Next time you go deeper \u2014 and
      deeper means you will run into something eventually."
    - Shoot it.
    inProgressLines:
    - bring me proof of your kill, or else i won't believe you.
    doneLines: []
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: FindLockedDoor
    quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4a36cfbcc57e82f4e95fe46bd23ea9fb, type: 2}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8b1ef5b631ffbeb4a838facc350e2886, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems: []
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - You shot something.
    - Good. That's what the gun is for.
    - "Now I need you going further in. Not the outer section \u2014 deeper. There's
      more in there and I need to know what. Keep exploring until you hit something
      you can't get past."
    inProgressLines:
    - So, still no blockers?
    doneLines: []
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: OpenTheDoor
    quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0dd4bdc5aff68b94eb7126c77fdbb4eb, type: 2}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4a36cfbcc57e82f4e95fe46bd23ea9fb, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems:
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5a8ca49cd692f41439eb081b13c42005, type: 2}
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - A locked door.
    - '*He nods slowly.*'
    - Of course there is.
    - '*He reaches into his coat and sets a key on the table.*'
    - Take it. See if it fits anything down there.
    inProgressLines:
    - Report to me when you find anything.
    doneLines: []
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: FindTheLab
    quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fa4564685abbcab4e9b09a103cadc672, type: 2}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0dd4bdc5aff68b94eb7126c77fdbb4eb, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems: []
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - So it fit.
    - He leans back.
    - Good. Then this should keep you busy for a while.
    - Go back in and keep looking. Every room, every corridor. I was told that key
      was needed to access a lab somewhere in that section. Find it and come back.
    inProgressLines:
    - Report to me when you find anything.
    doneLines: []
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: Lab2A
    quest: {fileID: 0}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fa4564685abbcab4e9b09a103cadc672, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems: []
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - Lab 2A
    - '*A pause. Something behind his eyes.*'
    - Is it locked?
    - Then I can't help you right now. I don't have a key for that door.
    - Keep working. If something comes up I'll let you know.
    inProgressLines:
    - Report to me when you find anything.
    doneLines: []
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: FindDocument
    quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0c079a8369ab76243a681303584c349b, type: 2}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: cf459ffa5e5fcf0418def9cab4303346, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bafc33bf6be91134aaef5f3c39edf404, type: 2}
    rewardItems: []
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - You found a way in?
    - '*He looks at the key. Doesn''t ask where it came from.*'
    - "Then go. Whatever is in that lab \u2014 documents, files, anything written
      down \u2014 bring it all to me. Every single thing you can carry out of there."
    - Don't try to understand it. Just bring it.
    inProgressLines:
    - Report to me when you find anything.
    doneLines: []
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: FinishContract
    quest: {fileID: 0}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0c079a8369ab76243a681303584c349b, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bafc33bf6be91134aaef5f3c39edf404, type: 2}
    rewardItems: []
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - '*He takes the documents. Reads in silence for a long moment.*'
    - ...Yes.
    - That's it. That's what I've been looking for.
    - '*He sets them down carefully. Like they''re fragile.*'
    - "With this \u2014 our contract is fulfilled."
    - '*He looks at you. For the first time, something in his expression is unguarded.*'
    - You're free.
    inProgressLines:
    - Report to me when you find anything.
    doneLines: []
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
