--- !u!114 &2074312301
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2074312297}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 673caeaf093b68d4aa06d0eab062bd3c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuestGiver
  _prompt: Talk
  _speakerName: Vera
  _defaultPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 71030eb1c5d46fa44a947dd39120c14c, type: 3}
  _idleLines:
  - I don't have anything for you right now.
  _stages:
  - label: kill3mob
    quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 111a96b1aa5979f409eca1aab2c62617, type: 2}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8b1ef5b631ffbeb4a838facc350e2886, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems:
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: be5e3b92a2a612d438abed965bb1af6c, type: 2}
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - So you found one of them.
    - "Those black things. Mimics, I call them \u2014 nobody else has bothered naming
      them, far as I know."
    - I've been watching people go down those stairs for a long time. Never got to
      hear back from anyone, they just never return.
    - "I've got work for you, if you want it. Real work \u2014 not whatever Marcus
      has you chasing. I need those things dead. As many as possible, as often as
      possible."
    - I'll pay in batteries. Good ones.
    - All you have to do is kill 3 of the pesky mimics.
    inProgressLines:
    - Return when you have proof you killed them.
    doneLines:
    - Great, now i can live with a slighly clearer mind.
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: FindIncubator
    quest: {fileID: 11400000, guid: cf459ffa5e5fcf0418def9cab4303346, type: 2}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 111a96b1aa5979f409eca1aab2c62617, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems: []
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - She slides a rechargeable battery across the bar.
    - "*A pause. She doesn't look satisfied \u2014 she looks like she's doing math
      in her head.*"
    - Here's what bothers me. I've had people kill these things before. And the numbers
      never go down. Kill three, next run there are five more waiting.
    - They're not coming in from outside. They're being made somewhere in there.
    - '*She looks at you.*'
    - Please tell me if you find any connection to where they migh come from.
    inProgressLines:
    - Please report to me when you find something
    doneLines:
    - Great, now i can live with a slighly clearer mind. Here's your promised Rechargable
      battery
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: AfterIncubatorFind
    quest: {fileID: 0}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: cf459ffa5e5fcf0418def9cab4303346, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems:
    - {fileID: 11400000, guid: ab72499d68db283448c0d952029cbadd, type: 2}
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - An incubator.
    - '*Long pause.*'
    - "Someone built them. Those things aren't accidents \u2014 someone made them
      and left the machine running."
    - '*She looks genuinely unsettled for the first time.*'
    - ...I think I can trust you with this.
    - '*She reaches into her jacket and sets a key on the bar. Old, worn. The label
      reads: Lab 2A.*'
    - I've had this for a while. Never knew what to do with it. Whoever left it with
      me didn't come back to explain.
    - "But an incubator down there, built by someone \u2014 can this be linked to
      all of it? I need you to find Lab 2A and tell me what you find."
    inProgressLines:
    - i hope you will be able to find something there.
    doneLines:
    - 
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
  - label: FindIncubator
    quest: {fileID: 0}
    requiresQuestBefore: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0c079a8369ab76243a681303584c349b, type: 2}
    turnInItem: {fileID: 0}
    rewardItems: []
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    offerLines:
    - You found it. What was in there?
    - '*You tell her.*'
    - Long silence.
    - ...So someone built all of it. The lab, the incubator, the mimics. All of it
      on purpose.
    - Does Marcus know about this?
    - Okay, youre free, im gonna settle this with Marcus
    inProgressLines:
    - i hope you will be able to find something there.
    doneLines:
    - 
    requireAcceptChoice: 0
